cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Agent Memory in research, architecture work, or an implementation, please cite the repository and preserve the relevant doctrine/provenance references."
title: "Agent Memory: A Reference Architecture for Governed Agentic Memory"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Knapp
    given-names: Kevin R.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Knapp-Kevin/agent-memory"
url: "https://github.com/Knapp-Kevin/agent-memory"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Agent Memory is a reference architecture for governed memory in autonomous
  and agentic systems, spanning memory theory, lifecycle, provenance,
  uncertainty, forgetting, recall governance, PAMA mutation authority,
  schemas, conformance fixtures, and implementation evidence.
keywords:
  - agentic memory
  - AI agents
  - memory governance
  - PAMA
  - provenance
  - conformance
  - long-term memory
  - forgetting
